# Application to All Classrooms

#### AI is becoming part of how students learn, communicate, and make decisions across all subjects. Students are already using AI for writing, research, and problem-solving, and it shapes the information and content they see every day. However, many students are using these tools without fully understanding how they work or their limitations.

#### AI connects to every subject across all grade levels.

#### 👉 Click on the cards below to learn more about how AI connects to your subject area(s).

<div style="max-width:1200px; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; color:#2f2f2f;">

<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4, 1fr); gap:14px;">

<!-- English -->
<details style="background:#ffffff; border:2px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 3px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
<summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:0; display:block;">
<div style="padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:10px;">English Language Arts</div>
<img src="https://images.code.org/48b2b90b61641cea37c5c1964fe6d142-Screenshot 2026-04-01 at 11.32.19 AM.png" style="width:100px; height:100px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
</summary>
<div style="padding:0 12px 12px 12px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.4;">
AI connects to reading, writing, speaking, and media literacy. Students can compare AI and human writing, examine voice and authorship, and evaluate when AI supports or weakens original thinking.
</div>
</details>

<!-- Social Studies -->
<details style="background:#ffffff; border:2px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 3px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
<summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:0; display:block;">
<div style="padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:10px;">Social Studies</div>
<img src="https://images.code.org/70f3a03bedace16c9af9afa35e6b2e40-Screenshot 2026-04-01 at 11.32.24 AM.png" style="width:100px; height:100px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
</summary>
<div style="padding:0 12px 12px 12px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.4;">
AI connects to history, civics, and society through bias, misinformation, and decision-making. Students can analyze how AI shapes information and impacts fairness in real-world systems.
</div>
</details>

<!-- Mathematics -->
<details style="background:#ffffff; border:2px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 3px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
<summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:0; display:block;">
<div style="padding:12px; text-align:center;">
<div style="font-size:16px; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:10px;">Mathematics</div>
<img src="https://images.code.org/6eaacd75c2b37e90bd177f1f4ddb962d-Screenshot 2026-04-01 at 11.32.28 AM.png" style="width:100px; height:100px; object-fit:contain;">
</div>
</summary>
<div style="padding:0 12px 12px 12px; font-size:14px; line-height:1.4;">
AI connects to math through patterns, probability, and data. Students can explore how AI makes predictions and why results depend on assumptions and data quality.
</div>
</details>

<!-- Science -->
<details style="background:#ffffff; border:2px solid #5a2ca0; border-radius:14px; overflow:hidden; box-shadow:0 3px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);">
<summary style="list-style:none; cursor:pointer; padding:0; display:block;">
